From d319bc78d73596f4e8d2904150f7a36b944825d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:19:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vu1: statically scheduled blocks in generated programs

Generated VU1 programs split each chunk into blocks: runs of consecutive
pairs with no branch, E/D/T bit, XGKICK or reserved instruction and nothing
pending from a branch. The generator runs each block through stepPairAfter
on a scratch VU from an idle pipeline to get every pair's issue cycle and the
ready cycles the block leaves; at run time a guard checks that nothing issued
before the block (register writes, FDIV/EFU results) can delay any pair, and
the block then runs without per-pair ready tracking, stall loops or budget
checks, writing the ready cycles once at the end. Otherwise the per-pair
code runs as before. GA2_VU1GEN_BLOCKS=0 turns blocks off.

ga2_vu1_check --reference: 0 mismatches on the Eigou 2 narration, Zettai
map and battle, and Mugen 1 tutorial captures; narration replay ~14 ->
~8.5 ns/VU cycle under the same (heavy) host load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
